 attacked the homes of the celestial  dragons in the holy land destroying a  monument of the divine dragon claw and  the symbol of the world nobles it was a  blatant declaration of war they say even  admirals aramaki and fujitora were not  enough to prevent the revolutionaries  from freeing kuma from celestial dragon  slavery aside from kobra's death  obviously which does suck the rest is  amazing to hear without dragon his  commanders clashed with two admirals and  succeeded yeah it probably wasn't a  decisive victory in terms of defeating  the admirals but even being able to hold  them back long enough to escape with  kuma is beyond impressive we're told  that princess vivi went missing which  will be a big mystery that needs to be  revealed for a while i'm sure but we do  know that imusama seemed to be after  vivi so there could be a connection  there and some people may well ask was  it blackbeard who again took advantage  of a commotion to get devin to  impersonate sabo and then kidnap vivi it  remains to be seen but as i mentioned in  the spoiler video it's possible that  blackbeard moved in to take over  alabasta after the rulers disappeared  we're then introduced to black horse the  navy criminal affairs unit chief and  these guys named with these color and  animal patterns are usually always op so  he's one to watch out for akainu says  alabasta is in chaos he bets again a  good opportunity for blackbeard to swoop  in we're really starting to understand  what aramaki was recently talking about  about the marines being in a bad  position and the world being in chaos  outside of wano kizaru mentions the  attempted murder of saint charlos and if  they can close the case of course this  was a super annoying dude luffy punched  in the most satisfying way possible  apparently though another celestial  dragon excuse the criminals akainu adds  that in the holy land the gods knights  have jurisdiction so he says to leave  the case to them it's interesting seeing  akainu in this position he definitely  seems to have changed since his admiral  days and no longer seems as hot-headed  and stubborn as before black horse says  most incidents are linked to sabo and  that his flames of rebellion are  spreading over the globe and yes how  perfect is that line flames of rebellion  for sabo who has the flame flame fruit  it's it's great i love that line it's  amazing we're told all eight of those  rebelling kingdoms were inspired to  stage their revolutionary coups while  their kings were still returning home he  says it's almost like they are  worshiping sabo as a god with the growth  of his legend they're saying his  influence is now greater than that of  dragon himself who as we all know is  sabo's leader pretty crazy stuff and i  gotta say i'm happy to see sabu's  reputation exploding including the  reputation of the revolutionaries in  general i'm glad sabo wasn't just left  behind in the dust by luffy in terms of  influence these brothers are killing it  and you love to see it and kizuru points  that out saying on top of that his  little brother has been dubbed a yonko  people are even citing luffy as just  another example of sabo's influence at  work in the pirate world they say sabo's  brother upended the status quo and right  now times are being forced to change  akainu actually comes off as really cool  here saying he became fleet admiral at a  crazy time but he doesn't care where  they attack from the marines will strike  back and return fire on all fronts it's  crazy to see the once overbearing and  powerful world government in a situation  like this it's also exciting when you  think about them the revolutionaries  shanks going for the one piece  blackbeard buggy and so on right now we  should all be thinking what a time to be  alive what a time to be a one piece fan  this is crazy amazing stuff chill the  pirate king within and smash that like  button if you enjoyed this review and  want to keep them coming be a smashing  p